  Rewrite by m0us3r - https://github.com/mym0us3r/Unified-Sysmon-Configs
  Date: 07/24/2026 Friday

  Sysmon Process Tampering rules: 100900 - 100910
  Rewritten for Sysmon Native (Windows 11 24H2+)
  Provider: Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon
  EID 25: ProcessTampering - Process Hollowing (T1055.012) and
          Process Herpaderping (T1055.013) detection
  MITRE ATT&CK v15 aligned

  ESCAPING REFERENCE (critical):
    Wazuh decoder doubles backslashes in Windows paths.
    Stored internally: C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmd.exe (double backslash)
    PCRE2 to match \\: use \\\\
    Rule: path separators -> \\\\ | regex meta (\s \d \b \.) -> \\

  CONTEXT:
    EID 25 was added in Sysmon v13 (2021) specifically to catch two
    process-tampering techniques: Hollowing (replacing a legitimate
    process's mapped image with malicious code) and Herpaderping
    (modifying the on-disk file after it has been mapped into memory,
    creating a mismatch between what's on disk and what's running).
    Both are classic defense-evasion techniques used to make malicious
    code appear as a trusted process in task lists and process trees.

  KNOWN LIMITATION - IMPORTANT, READ BEFORE DEPLOYING:
    This event does NOT detect the full family of related techniques.
    Process Ghosting (a newer variant documented by Elastic Security)
    is specifically designed to evade the exact detection window EID 25
    relies on - it deletes the backing file before Sysmon's check can
    run. EID 25 catches Hollowing and Herpaderping; it is not a
    catch-all for this technique class. Layer with other detections
    (e.g. 0870 CreateRemoteThread, 0850 parent/image anomaly chain).

    The sysmon-native.xml Type field values ("Image is replaced" for
    Hollowing, "Image is locked for access" for Herpaderping) were
    corrected on 2026-07-24 based on documentation from TrustedSec's
    SysmonCommunityGuide and a captured real EID 25 event example
    (ultimatewindowssecurity.com) - NOT confirmed against a live event
    on this project's own endpoint, since no EID 25 has fired here yet.
    If the field values turn out to be wrong once a real event is
    captured, both the Sysmon config AND this file's field references
    would need correction.

  MIGRATION NOTES:
    ANCHOR: if_group>sysmon_event_25, assigned by rule 100851 in
    0595-win-sysmon_rules.xml. Rule ID chosen directly in the officially
    reserved custom-rule range (100000-120000) from the start - not
    reused from the 61xxx sequence, avoiding the mistake documented in
    0595's header regarding this exact slot.
    This is a NEW file - not yet field-tested (no live EID 25 event
    available to validate against on this endpoint). Validate with
    wazuh-analysisd -t and, if a controlled Hollowing/Herpaderping test
    can be safely run, a live field test before treating as
    production-confirmed - consistent with every other rule in this
    project.
-->

<group name="sysmon,sysmon_eid25,windows,">

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       BASE ANCHOR - EID 25 (Process Tampering)
       Low-volume, high-value event by design (Sysmon's own
       documentation describes it as such) - anchor kept at level 0
       per this project's dominant convention; the event itself
       reaching Wazuh at all is already a strong signal, but the
       child rules below carry the actual severity.
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <rule id="100900" level="0">
    <if_group>sysmon_event_25</if_group>
    <field name="win.system.providerName">^Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon$</field>
    <description>Native Sysmon [EID 25]: Process tampering detected - $(win.eventdata.image)</description>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
  </rule>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       T1055.012 - Process Hollowing
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <rule id="100901" level="15">
    <if_sid>100900</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.type" type="pcre2">(?i)Image is replaced</field>
    <description>CRITICAL: Process Hollowing detected - $(win.eventdata.image) image replaced in memory</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1055.012</id>
    </mitre>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
  </rule>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       T1055.013 - Process Herpaderping
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <rule id="100902" level="15">
    <if_sid>100900</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.type" type="pcre2">(?i)Image is locked for access</field>
    <description>CRITICAL: Process Herpaderping detected - $(win.eventdata.image) on-disk image tampered post-mapping</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1055.013</id>
    </mitre>
    <options>no_full_log</options>
  </rule>

</group>
